.TH AX25CHESS 1 "October 2026" "AX25Chess" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ax25chess \- chess over AX.25 packet radio with a built-in Dire Wolf modem
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ax25chess
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-modem\-conf\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-modem\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ax25chess
plays chess between two amateur radio stations over AX.25 UI frames. A move
travels as the unique identifier of the piece and the number of the
destination square; every move carries a fingerprint of the resulting
position, so a divergence is caught within one half-move and repaired by
replaying the history (the CHS-1 protocol, see
\fI/usr/share/doc/ax25chess/PROTOCOL.md\fR). The modem is Dire Wolf, compiled
into the program: a sound card and a PTT line are all the hardware needed.
.PP
The modem is configured in Settings: sound card, speed, PTT and channel
access; the program writes the matching \fIdirewolf.conf\fR to
\fI~/.config/AX25Chess/\fR. A Dire Wolf configuration file of one's own can
be used instead. Settings are kept in \fI~/.config/AX25Chess/config.json\fR,
games in progress in \fI~/.local/share/AX25Chess/games/\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Use this settings file instead of the default.
.TP
.BI \-\-modem\-conf " PATH"
Start the modem with this \fIdirewolf.conf\fR, for this run only.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-modem
Do not start the modem at start-up, whatever the settings say.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show the options and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/AX25Chess/config.json
The settings.
.TP
.I ~/.config/AX25Chess/direwolf.conf
The modem configuration generated from the settings.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/AX25Chess/games/
One file per game in progress, the move list in compact form.
.SH NOTES
A PTT through the GPIO of a CM108 USB sound card needs write access to its
hidraw device; the package installs a udev rule giving it to the
\fIaudio\fR group.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR direwolf (1)
